9:     """Complete the dominant-color object by adding its left-right mirror image.
10: 
11:     Input structure
12:     A rectangular grid contains one uniquely most frequent color forming the main
13:     foreground object, with other colors acting as clutter/noise.
14: 
15:     Rule
16:     Reflect every pixel of the dominant color across the vertical centerline of
17:     the grid and recolor the reflected cells with that same dominant color.
18: 
19:     Key insight
20:     The noisy cells are exactly the missing counterpart pixels needed to make the
21:     dominant-color mask horizontally symmetric.
22:     """
